            <div xml:id="d227">

                <pb facs="0171" n="163" sameAs="frus:frus1939v05/pg163"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">715.1715/1427: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Representative of the President</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Corrigan</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1939-05-24T19:00:00-04:00">May 24, 1939—7
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>46. Your telegrams No. 53, May 19, 11 a.m., and No. 55, May 22, 4 p.m. In view of
                    reports that President Somoza intends to visit Tegucigalpa in order to discuss
                    with President Carías a possible solution of the boundary problem, I do not
                    consider it wise for the Commission or Mr. Ocheltree to take any action at this
                    time. Ocheltree’s proposed visit to Tegucigalpa should therefore be
                    deferred.</p>
                <p>I think that the Commission should bear in mind the possibility of carrying out
                    the visit following the conversation between the two presidents if it then
                    appears that the visit should be desirable.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
